Features/Optional Features
Note: The agent itself is lightweight and fixed; optional features are relevant only from the perspective of Azure Backup service capabilities.

Azure BackInt agent works seamlessly with Azure backup service; 

Supports Full, Differential, Incremental and Log backups, Snapshots - (with daily maximum limits)

OOTB Standard 15-minute Recovery Point Objective (RPO): Recovery of critical data of up to 15 minutes is possible using Azure Backup service. FAQ — Back up SAP HANA databases on Azure VMs - Azure Backup

Optional: One-click, point-in-time restores via HANA Studio: Restore of production data can be done on alternate HANA servers. Chaining of backups and catalogs to perform restores is all managed by Azure behind the scenes.
About the SAP HANA database backup on Azure VMs - Azure Backup
Restore SAP HANA databases on Azure VMs - Azure Backup

By Design, Azure Backint agent always uses secure (TLS) communication even if SSL Enforce is disabled in HANA. 

SAP HANA can encrypt the Backint backup data streams using TLS/SSL (TLS 1.2 in transit, encrypted at rest using MMK). 

As of May 2026, Microsoft confirmed there is no official documentation stating Azure Backup for SAP HANA supports or is validated with TLS 1.3

Optional: SSL Enforce is an SAP HANA setting, not an Azure requirement; Azure Backup does not require SSL Enforce to be enabled

