Application / Supply Chain Integration
Azure Backint agent lifecycle is fully managed by Azure Backup with installation of the agent

Customer will need to work with Cloud team to operationalize Azure Backint agent; work with Customer SAP team to confirm Azure Backint is restoring and backing up to Azure Backup Recovery Services Vault

Lifecycle Management
Lifecycle management of the Azure BackInt agent is controlled by Microsoft and is done continuously, not just at the time of installation

Every time a backup operation is orchestrated, Azure Backup validates:

SAP HANA version (SPS + revision)

OS version (RHEL/SLES + minor level)

HSR role (primary/secondary)

Azure Backup BackInt version

Backint Agent compatible metadata (specific to SAP products like HANA, ECC , Solution Manager etc.)

Azure’s BackInt agent version is automatically chosen, updated and patched based on the parameters mentioned above, unless the Customer wants to use an older/specific version of Agent to support an older/specific HANA version for example. However, the version of the Azure BackInt Agent used must be the standard across the organization.

Note: 

SAP outlines Azure Backup BackInt version requirements in the SAP Note: 2756788 - Support Process Microsoft Azure Backup BackInt

SAP outlines the Azure BackInt Agent version 1.1 as the last approved/certified & still supported by SAP in the SAP Note: 3639106 - Certification on MS Azure backup 2.0

